WEBVTT

00:00.660 --> 00:02.020
<i>Summer vacation.</i>

00:02.020 --> 00:06.940
<i>The season when everyone grows, 
regardless of status or age.</i>

00:07.350 --> 00:12.460
<i>Misumi Makoto sets his own goals 
and steps out into the summer sun.</i>

00:13.890 --> 00:16.140
Are you serious?

00:16.140 --> 00:18.650
I meant 100% of what I said.

00:19.250 --> 00:20.870
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:20.870 --> 00:27.430
You have far more mana than me, 
and yet you still want more?

00:27.430 --> 00:31.350
No, no. I want to increase the amount 
of mana I can expend at once.

00:31.350 --> 00:33.250
My, uh... output, I guess?

00:33.740 --> 00:36.350
Right now, I feel like I'm really inefficient.

00:36.350 --> 00:41.760
Listen, in most cases, there isn't anything 
people can do to increase their own mana.

00:42.100 --> 00:45.650
But my maximum mana seems to have increased.

00:45.940 --> 00:49.180
If a research organization 
found out about that,

00:49.180 --> 00:51.870
they'd cut you up and experiment on you.

00:51.870 --> 00:53.160
Seriously?

00:53.160 --> 00:57.870
Seriously. Heck, I'd like to know 
how you've increased it, too.

00:58.770 --> 01:02.040
All I do is draw a bow every day.

01:02.040 --> 01:06.820
Yeah, yeah. If you insist, then I 
should have something around here.

01:07.090 --> 01:08.320
Here it is.

01:08.320 --> 01:09.170
What's this?

01:09.510 --> 01:11.930
Training methods related to mana.

01:11.930 --> 01:14.180
I don't know if they're effective, though.

01:14.180 --> 01:15.950
Ooh, thanks!

01:15.950 --> 01:20.500
You're a teacher and a merchant, 
and yet you're as studious as a student.

01:20.890 --> 01:24.890
Maybe it's because the 
academy's on summer break.

01:25.390 --> 01:28.130
I always felt restless before 
breaks and looked forward

01:28.130 --> 01:30.530
to planning how I'd spend my time.

01:30.530 --> 01:33.890
I just felt like doing a bunch of things.

01:35.860 --> 01:39.940
There's nothing wrong 
with remembering the past.

01:39.940 --> 01:43.650
I pray you have a wonderful summer vacation.

02:09.020 --> 02:11.560
<b>Season Two</b>

03:16.120 --> 03:18.920
<b>Night Eleven   Summer of Growth and New Skills</b>

03:16.120 --> 03:18.920
<b>Night Eleven   Summer of Growth and New Skills</b>

03:19.040 --> 03:21.000
You seem busy.

03:21.420 --> 03:26.100
I hear you're training your 
students over summer break.

03:26.100 --> 03:28.260
<i>They're all such motivated kids.</i>

03:28.600 --> 03:32.330
Most full-time instructors have 
gone on vacation or returned home.

03:32.330 --> 03:34.560
Not many teachers are like you.

03:34.910 --> 03:37.640
Personally, I like that sort of teacher, though.

03:37.950 --> 03:39.800
<i>Thank you.</i>

03:39.800 --> 03:42.780
<i>Anyway, you said you found 
a book to recommend to me.</i>

03:42.780 --> 03:45.010
Yes. This is it.

03:45.010 --> 03:47.940
<i>Is this... an essay?</i>

03:48.400 --> 03:53.270
Yes. You seemed interested 
in the use of mana,

03:53.270 --> 03:55.790
so I found this unusual text for you.

03:56.700 --> 04:02.100
<i>The potential for physical interference of 
mana, from the perspective of visualization.</i>

04:02.510 --> 04:07.630
It's an essay based on unique theories 
that only true connoisseurs can appreciate.

04:08.020 --> 04:10.850
<i>In other words, it's for hardcore nerds.</i>

04:11.250 --> 04:13.830
<i>It certainly sounds interesting.</i>

04:14.400 --> 04:17.180
<i>I have yet another goal 
for this summer break.</i>

04:17.180 --> 04:19.700
Goals for summer break?

04:20.730 --> 04:23.410
You sound like a student.

04:23.410 --> 04:26.690
<i>Well, I am a student.</i>

04:28.180 --> 04:29.580
Young Master!

04:29.950 --> 04:32.530
<i>How time flies.</i>

04:32.930 --> 04:36.710
<i>Essays, training, and managerial duties.</i>

04:37.570 --> 04:40.590
<i>Summer in the demiplane 
flew by like an arrow,</i>

04:40.590 --> 04:43.920
<i>and before I knew it, two weeks had passed.</i>

04:43.920 --> 04:51.450
I'm sorry you're busy every day 
with approvals and daily reports.

04:51.450 --> 04:56.660
It's fine. Once the academy's summer 
break ends, I'll be busy again.

04:56.660 --> 05:00.090
I'd like to spend as much 
time with everyone as I can.

05:00.090 --> 05:02.120
I'm glad to hear you say that.

05:02.120 --> 05:06.680
We're blessed to have a master like you.

05:06.680 --> 05:07.560
Emma-san?

05:10.050 --> 05:12.070
Let's get started on today's schedule.

05:12.070 --> 05:13.780
Oh, I'm sorry!

05:15.140 --> 05:19.410
Today, you have a mock battle 
against the wingkin.

05:19.750 --> 05:24.480
They've already fought the 
orcs and others several times,

05:24.480 --> 05:26.270
and they're undefeated so far.

05:26.270 --> 05:28.630
Huh. They must be pretty strong.

05:28.630 --> 05:31.730
Their ability to fly is 
a significant advantage.

05:31.730 --> 05:35.180
But with a few more battles...

05:35.690 --> 05:38.590
We orcs won't keep losing.

05:38.590 --> 05:41.720
O-Oh, yeah? I'd better pull 
myself together, too.

05:43.030 --> 05:46.400
So... where are the wingkin?

05:46.400 --> 05:51.480
In those woods. The battle begins 
with both sides out of sight.

05:51.480 --> 05:53.470
Good luck.

05:55.970 --> 05:57.890
<i>How should I begin?</i>

06:01.890 --> 06:03.670
<i>First, I'll say hello.</i>

06:05.340 --> 06:07.500
<i>After firing the first shot, I'll—</i>

06:08.710 --> 06:10.000
All my shots hit?!

06:10.270 --> 06:11.910
A-All units have taken fire!

06:11.910 --> 06:13.740
We're taking more fire than expected!

06:13.740 --> 06:15.020
Second wave, advance!

06:15.620 --> 06:16.730
Yeesh.

06:17.010 --> 06:21.220
<i>With no way to handle long-range 
attacks and such a weak defense...</i>

06:21.560 --> 06:23.500
All squads, take your positions.

06:24.470 --> 06:28.070
<i>I see. That certainly 
obstructs my vision, but...</i>

06:28.730 --> 06:29.960
<i>Investigative Kai.</i>

06:33.500 --> 06:35.450
<i>Yup, now they're sitting ducks.</i>

06:36.740 --> 06:38.250
Prepare for falling debris!

06:38.250 --> 06:40.320
Deploy magical barriers!

06:40.320 --> 06:44.830
<i>Emma said they were strong, 
but they're just flying targets.</i>

06:46.550 --> 06:47.850
<i>Is that...</i>

06:48.720 --> 06:50.630
<i>It's Chief Kakun.</i>

06:51.000 --> 06:52.690
<i>Then that bird must be...</i>

06:53.590 --> 06:55.400
<i>His lieutenant, Shona-san.</i>

06:55.400 --> 06:59.850
<i>Come to think of it, wingkin can 
transform into large birds.</i>

07:00.280 --> 07:02.410
<i>How will they deal with long-range attacks?</i>

07:04.610 --> 07:07.650
<i>Good. That's what I was hoping to see.</i>

07:09.690 --> 07:11.330
<i>Enhancement and wind?</i>

07:11.330 --> 07:13.250
<i>Are they planning a suicide attack?</i>

07:13.250 --> 07:17.820
<i>Maybe the security of being airborne 
has simplified their attacks.</i>

07:26.130 --> 07:28.250
A straight line is too predictable.

07:28.520 --> 07:29.750
I-I'm not done yet!

07:34.370 --> 07:36.730
W-We surrender.

07:39.500 --> 07:45.560
Since that was our first mock battle, 
I wanted to see how you fight.

07:45.560 --> 07:49.240
But to be honest, you rely too 
much on your ability to fly.

07:50.290 --> 07:55.460
In the near future, the highland orcs 
and others will crush you in battle.

07:55.710 --> 07:57.400
We'll crush you.

07:57.700 --> 07:59.980
You should stop launching 
suicide attacks, too.

08:00.400 --> 08:04.380
They make you easy prey 
for concentrated fire.

08:05.090 --> 08:07.710
Taking up positions in the sky

08:07.710 --> 08:10.920
and developing several attack 
patterns that are likely to succeed

08:10.920 --> 08:12.590
will be your starting point.

08:13.090 --> 08:15.590
That's all for today. Farewell.

08:15.590 --> 08:17.300
Y-Young Master.

08:17.620 --> 08:19.180
What is it?

08:19.640 --> 08:22.540
We'd also like to participate 
in developing and exploring

08:22.540 --> 08:24.770
the land and the demiplane ranking.

08:24.770 --> 08:29.560
Anyone can participate in the 
demiplane ranking at their own risk.

08:29.830 --> 08:33.950
But I can't allow you to 
develop the demiplane.

08:34.670 --> 08:38.330
Your combat abilities make 
you unsuited for the job.

08:38.330 --> 08:40.390
I see.

08:40.390 --> 08:44.300
For now, work on developing your strength.

08:46.930 --> 08:51.640
"In other words, when continuously 
releasing a large amount of mana,

08:51.640 --> 08:56.800
as a secondary effect, 
colorful mana manifests as a weak barrier,

08:56.800 --> 08:59.650
meaning mana becomes visible 
according to the volume released,

09:00.050 --> 09:04.100
and it may even materialize 
and become possible to touch."

09:04.360 --> 09:05.560
Wait, what?

09:06.870 --> 09:10.470
It's no use. My head's going to burst.

09:13.790 --> 09:18.420
<i>Just releasing mana is simple enough.</i>

09:22.870 --> 09:27.380
<i>I'll keep firing Brids while 
unleashing large amounts of mana.</i>

09:29.050 --> 09:32.330
<i>Using my own mana to 
maintain this output level</i>

09:32.330 --> 09:35.160
<i>feels like removing the barrier 
between me and my mana.</i>

09:35.160 --> 09:38.980
<i>Focus, focus, focus.</i>

09:45.710 --> 09:47.310
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

09:48.420 --> 09:51.750
<i>Huh? What's happening to me?</i>

09:55.900 --> 09:58.220
Young Master. Young Master.

09:58.220 --> 09:59.350
Young Master!

09:59.900 --> 10:00.530
Eh?

10:00.800 --> 10:01.650
Huh?!

10:02.150 --> 10:05.740
You weren't in your room this morning, so...

10:06.080 --> 10:08.350
What were you doing?

10:08.350 --> 10:11.740
You're not the type of man to 
get drunk and sleep outdoors.

10:11.740 --> 10:12.700
Oh, right.

10:13.030 --> 10:16.170
I'm... Misumi Makoto.

10:16.170 --> 10:19.590
Yes, we know that already.

10:19.590 --> 10:23.640
Yes, you are Misumi Makoto-sama, my master.

10:24.010 --> 10:27.070
<i>So I spent all night firing Brids.</i>

10:27.760 --> 10:31.100
<i>Come to think of it, 
I believe this has happened before...</i>

10:38.620 --> 10:42.320
Tomoe and Mio, thanks for all your help.

10:42.320 --> 10:43.530
Huh?

10:43.880 --> 10:44.710
Huh?

10:45.080 --> 10:47.760
It's nothing. Let's head back.

10:54.030 --> 10:56.290
Breakfast looks delicious as always, Mio.

10:56.290 --> 11:01.430
I'm working diligently to learn how 
to cook everything while you're here.

11:01.750 --> 11:06.140
Young Master, might I have a bit of 
that persimmon and mashed tofu salad?

11:06.520 --> 11:09.850
Tomoe-san, limit yourself 
to your own portion.

11:09.850 --> 11:11.760
It's your fault for making something

11:11.760 --> 11:15.170
that goes so well with sake 
first thing in the morning!

11:15.810 --> 11:19.610
Tomoe, why don't you cut back a little?

11:19.610 --> 11:23.750
In your country, they say it's worth 
selling the farm to enjoy a morning drink.

11:26.160 --> 11:28.170
This goes fantastic with sake, too!

11:29.330 --> 11:31.940
Those are persimmons in mirin.

11:31.940 --> 11:36.580
It'd be even better if you made 
real mirin for me, Tomoe-san.

11:37.080 --> 11:39.540
I'm working on miso and mirin right now.

11:39.880 --> 11:43.360
Tomoe, you sure do love the 
demiplane's persimmons.

11:43.360 --> 11:45.250
Indeed I do.

11:45.250 --> 11:49.120
So much that I think about being buried 
in a mountain of persimmons someday.

11:49.120 --> 11:50.350
Don't waste your thoughts on that.

11:51.060 --> 11:56.320
Tomoe-san, if you don't behave, 
I'll stop serving persimmons.

11:57.780 --> 11:59.230
<b>Several Days Later</b>

12:01.030 --> 12:05.670
<i>I've finally learned to utilize 
the mana outside my body, too.</i>

12:09.400 --> 12:11.990
<i>I won't enter a trance-like state again.</i>

12:12.670 --> 12:14.540
<i>This time...</i>

12:15.400 --> 12:20.500
<i>There was an incantation at the end of the 
essay that might make mana materialize.</i>

12:21.080 --> 12:23.900
<i>It works similarly to the 
common starch experiment.</i>

12:24.410 --> 12:26.100
<i>The stronger you hit it, 
the harder it becomes.</i>

12:26.700 --> 12:30.000
<i>Touch it gently, and it remains a liquid.</i>

12:30.940 --> 12:35.060
<i>First, I'll use Concealing Kai to hide my mana.</i>

12:35.760 --> 12:38.820
<i>Kazukurani shizumaruyomichi.</i>

12:38.820 --> 12:44.150
<i>Bandaika katashirowaniwa sankuaregoshi.</i>

12:45.390 --> 12:48.660
<i>It's okay. I have plenty of mana to spare.</i>

12:48.660 --> 12:51.360
<i>Now, show me the results.</i>

12:56.770 --> 12:58.920
<i>Is this mana's physical form?</i>

13:00.310 --> 13:01.080
<i>Yeah.</i>

13:02.410 --> 13:04.220
<i>It's following my movements.</i>

13:04.920 --> 13:07.130
<i>If I fire a Brid now...</i>

13:10.090 --> 13:13.650
<i>Okay. I successfully used 
the mana outside my body.</i>

13:14.150 --> 13:15.610
<i>This is efficient.</i>

13:15.610 --> 13:17.730
<i>Next, how strong is its surface?</i>

13:23.730 --> 13:26.160
<i>Well, that didn't hurt at all.</i>

13:26.160 --> 13:28.030
<i>If it's this strong,</i>

13:28.570 --> 13:31.060
<i>I should be able to fight 
anyone from goddesses</i>

13:31.060 --> 13:33.670
<i>to dragon slayers without 
suffering serious injury.</i>

13:35.680 --> 13:39.510
<i>For the demiplane's sake, I cannot fall.</i>

13:40.430 --> 13:43.210
<i>If someone has to die, 
I'd rather it be just me.</i>

13:43.210 --> 13:48.760
<i>I don't want to drag anyone who 
loves me into this conflict.</i>

13:50.830 --> 13:53.760
<i>And so, half my summer break passed.</i>

13:54.880 --> 13:57.220
A demonstration of the 
races' new combat skills?

13:57.700 --> 14:03.690
Like your students, the denizens of the 
demiplane have been training daily.

14:04.080 --> 14:08.690
They'd like to show you 
what they've learned.

14:08.690 --> 14:12.440
Okay, sure, but what's that?

14:11.150 --> 14:12.440
Giant boulder!

14:11.160 --> 14:15.370
<b>Giant Boulder</b>

14:12.440 --> 14:15.370
I dug it out of a mountain.

14:15.860 --> 14:19.780
And I cast a special spell upon it.

14:19.780 --> 14:23.230
And everyone unleashes 
their new skills on it?

14:23.230 --> 14:26.700
Its power is expressed as a number.

14:27.180 --> 14:30.260
I'm not interested in new combat skills.

14:30.260 --> 14:32.750
I'd prefer a cooking contest instead.

14:33.740 --> 14:36.340
Leave some for everyone else.

14:39.110 --> 14:41.100
First up, the highland orcs.

14:41.380 --> 14:44.080
Agares and Emma, begin!

14:44.770 --> 14:47.020
Huh. Emma's participating, too?

14:47.400 --> 14:50.950
She's the highland orcs' greatest mage.

14:50.950 --> 14:53.000
She just handles miscellaneous 
duties more often.

14:53.390 --> 14:54.750
We won't hold back.

14:55.150 --> 14:56.660
Accept this spell!

15:01.540 --> 15:03.240
Seventy-eight points!

15:05.200 --> 15:10.900
Seventy-eight points? That's nearly 
a test score you'd be happy to receive.

15:10.900 --> 15:13.050
No, that's actually quite good.

15:13.050 --> 15:17.180
If that's your standard, then I 
feel sorry for the other species.

15:17.740 --> 15:20.850
Next, mist lizards. Begin!

15:24.970 --> 15:25.850
Huh?

15:25.850 --> 15:27.520
What are they aiming at?

15:28.070 --> 15:30.570
Perhaps they're showing 
off to the wingkin.

15:30.570 --> 15:34.030
"We've acquired a long-range 
attack that reaches the skies."

15:40.150 --> 15:41.910
Sixty-eight points!

15:43.060 --> 15:46.840
Next, the elder dwarves. Begin!

15:48.590 --> 15:50.670
That tiny axe can't possibly...

15:52.500 --> 15:53.130
Huh?

15:53.480 --> 15:54.510
Well, well.

15:54.770 --> 15:56.400
Mountain Cleaver.

16:00.120 --> 16:01.840
Seventy points!

16:03.820 --> 16:06.820
There's still room for improvement.

16:06.820 --> 16:09.390
It's not yet worthy of the 
name "Mountain Cleaver."

16:09.710 --> 16:12.370
Next, the alke. Sixty-five points!

16:12.740 --> 16:14.330
Next, the gorgons.

16:15.470 --> 16:19.040
Well, yeah. Turning a rock into 
stone will net you zero points.

16:19.400 --> 16:21.000
Finally, the wingkin.

16:23.270 --> 16:27.870
They're marking targets from the 
ground and bombing them from above.

16:28.390 --> 16:33.800
It's pretty accurate, 
but it still lacks power.

16:33.800 --> 16:35.510
Next, the forest ogres...

16:35.840 --> 16:36.660
Hey, wait.

16:37.100 --> 16:38.470
Why are you dressed like that?

16:38.470 --> 16:40.410
We can't wear anything more revealing.

16:40.410 --> 16:43.380
This is as much as our confidence allows.

16:43.380 --> 16:45.430
Even for you, we struggle to do more.

16:45.430 --> 16:46.890
What?

16:46.890 --> 16:48.900
Aqua, let's do this!

16:48.900 --> 16:50.240
I want to die.

16:50.240 --> 16:53.450
Utterly invincible, kills with a touch!

16:53.450 --> 16:57.630
Super crazy barrier of 
absolute zero, Cocytus!

16:58.130 --> 17:00.610
Killer Floral...

17:00.610 --> 17:03.040
Tribute!

17:08.680 --> 17:10.800
Now that's impressive.

17:10.800 --> 17:12.620
Not bad.

17:13.250 --> 17:15.550
<i>Break it if you can.</i>

17:15.860 --> 17:16.750
What?!

17:16.750 --> 17:18.290
Are you trying to provoke us?!

17:18.290 --> 17:19.940
Don't underestimate us!

17:22.240 --> 17:23.520
My weapon!

17:23.520 --> 17:26.480
It's remarkably offensive for a barrier.

17:26.820 --> 17:29.450
It might actually be capable 
of killing someone.

17:29.450 --> 17:32.490
It would take even me a 
while to break through it.

17:33.210 --> 17:35.950
As a barrier, it's nearly perfect.

17:37.060 --> 17:38.320
Really?

17:40.290 --> 17:42.420
<i>What's wrong? Bring it on.</i>

17:42.290 --> 17:44.880
<i>Huh? It's not perfect at all.</i>

17:42.420 --> 17:44.880
<i>You scared, huh? C'mon.</i>

17:45.260 --> 17:47.950
<i>What? Can't anyone break through it?</i>

17:48.330 --> 17:50.400
There. I got through it.

17:51.190 --> 17:52.770
Y-Young Master?

17:52.770 --> 17:54.310
B-B-B-B-But how?

17:54.310 --> 17:58.720
It's certainly impressive, 
but it's lacking something.

17:59.080 --> 18:03.440
Consider its shortcomings carefully. 
I'm going to dispel it now.

18:05.990 --> 18:07.270
Fifty points?

18:07.270 --> 18:10.100
What? A bonus stage?

18:10.410 --> 18:12.320
Now it's my turn.

18:12.320 --> 18:15.890
I thought you said you weren't 
interested in new combat skills.

18:15.890 --> 18:19.400
I'm not, but I didn't want 
to miss this opportunity.

18:19.850 --> 18:24.040
I thought I'd demonstrate my 
other hobby besides cooking.

18:24.040 --> 18:28.030
Are you talking about whatever you 
were watching in the memory vault?

18:28.570 --> 18:32.720
<i>Within the intensity, 
I can sense refinement.</i>

18:32.720 --> 18:38.290
<i>Delicate and powerful, a form that 
calls to mind spiders or insects.</i>

18:38.290 --> 18:40.950
<i>Oh, it's marvelous.</i>

18:41.750 --> 18:46.880
I based it on the figure from your memory.

18:47.350 --> 18:49.680
It's still only a prototype, but...

18:50.920 --> 18:52.470
I made this.

18:52.470 --> 18:54.890
A h-hero suit?

18:56.910 --> 18:58.160
No reaction.

18:58.160 --> 19:00.520
It's time for the final entry.

19:00.520 --> 19:03.670
Our Shiki has arrived!

19:03.980 --> 19:07.780
He seems to have acquired 
his own new ability.

19:07.780 --> 19:09.740
Let's see what it can do.

19:10.090 --> 19:12.370
I'm looking forward to it, too.

19:12.370 --> 19:15.410
Come, Thirteen Steps.

19:16.340 --> 19:19.140
Release steps one through three.

19:19.650 --> 19:23.340
Wand, Sword, Cup, Coin.

19:24.690 --> 19:25.810
Well, well.

19:26.050 --> 19:32.260
Worthy of the sixth step, 
unsheathe yourself and show your true self.

19:36.700 --> 19:40.200
Didn't the dwarves make 
that weapon for him?

19:40.500 --> 19:44.070
They insolently made it 
effective against dragons.

19:44.070 --> 19:46.820
I believe they called it a dragon slayer.

19:46.820 --> 19:51.070
Is he expecting a battle against 
Mitsurugi... against Lancer?

19:51.070 --> 19:54.130
Now you've done it, Shiki.

20:04.040 --> 20:08.320
It's not only effective against dragons, 
but it's physically powerful, too.

20:08.830 --> 20:10.240
Nice going, Shiki.

20:11.290 --> 20:14.230
It's all for nothing if he 
can't hit anything with it.

20:14.730 --> 20:18.400
Shiki's been watching your and 
Mio's progress and training, too.

20:18.700 --> 20:21.650
You should be glad to 
be a role model for him.

20:23.180 --> 20:26.170
Maybe I'll end this by 
showing off a skill, too.

20:26.170 --> 20:26.860
What?

20:26.860 --> 20:29.110
It'll be a surprise.

20:31.010 --> 20:35.080
Everyone, the young master will now 
demonstrate a new skill for us.

20:35.080 --> 20:36.660
Feast your eyes.

20:37.860 --> 20:39.090
Young Master!

20:39.090 --> 20:40.040
You're the best!

20:40.040 --> 20:42.620
Take it easy, everyone.

20:42.620 --> 20:46.350
I just discovered an interesting 
application of mana.

20:47.900 --> 20:53.900
<i>This will be my first time releasing a large 
amount of mana without Concealing Kai.</i>

20:57.120 --> 20:59.060
Wh-What is this?

20:59.060 --> 21:02.890
<i>Focus, focus, focus.</i>

21:06.440 --> 21:12.660
His mana materialized into its 
densest form, mana matter?

21:13.260 --> 21:15.040
Mana matter?

21:15.040 --> 21:17.260
I like that name.

21:17.530 --> 21:22.680
It strengthens my spells and 
functions as powerful armor.

21:23.000 --> 21:25.210
This is mana matter!

21:37.020 --> 21:39.600
So, what do you think?

21:42.440 --> 21:45.400
<b>Huh?</b>

21:42.820 --> 21:45.400
What is this?!

21:45.800 --> 21:47.130
<i>Over summer break</i>

21:47.130 --> 21:48.700
<i>I alone overdid it</i>

21:48.700 --> 21:50.140
<i>due to excitement.</i>

21:50.750 --> 21:53.780
What a tremendous current of mana.

21:54.480 --> 21:57.920
Is that a threat to us?

21:57.920 --> 22:02.870
Who knows? Either way, 
we must do something about it.

23:35.690 --> 23:38.930
Night Twelve: "Attack 
of the Giant Monsters."

23:35.970 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Time</b>

23:37.100 --> 23:39.930
<b>Attack of the Giant Monsters</b>
